Summary 

The goal is to distill history events to have the required info for predicting subsequent events with counterfactual analysis where events in history may have a causal relationship with the events observed later; 

The authors propose MTPP Counterfactual History Distiller (MTPP-CHD), which learns to select the optimal event combination from history for the events observed later. 

It is expected distilled events would have essential information but empirical results show otherwise; to address limitation, they add one more constraint to enforce that distilled events are informative; 

Authors claim: 
a) to distill a minimum subset of history events with the essential information for predicting the subsequent events using MTPP; 
b) Show CHD limitations on classical counterfactual approach and add constraint; 
c) proposed MTPP_CHD with gumbel-softmax trick;

Contributions can be splitted into three components: 
1) History distiller, encoder-decoder transformer, p(y|Hf,x0)
2) Historical event picker 
3) Training loss

